# /etc/my.cnf.d/zz-rds-include.cnf — Spinifex RDS generated-configuration include.
#
# The generated files live on the data volume rather than under /etc. A class
# change is a VM replacement: a fresh boot volume from this AMI with the same
# data volume reattached. Parameters under /etc would be discarded by that
# replacement and the instance would silently revert to catalog defaults while
# the API still reported the customer's values.
#
# zz- so this is the last drop-in the packaged !includedir reads. MariaDB walks
# an include directory in byte order and takes the last occurrence of a setting,
# which is what makes a platform-owned value beat a distribution default — and a
# digit prefix would sort ahead of the packaged mariadb-server.cnf rather than
# after it. setup.sh asserts the resulting order at build time.
#
# The directory is also baked empty into this image. MariaDB treats an
# !includedir it cannot open as a fatal defaults-parsing error, so a boot with no
# data volume mounted would otherwise take the client down with the server.

!includedir /var/lib/mysql/conf.d
